              "id": "CVE-2026-21895",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RSA: RSA crate: Denial of Service due to malformed prime in private key generation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The `rsa` crate is an RSA implementation written in rust. Prior to version 0.9.10, when creating a RSA private key from its components, the construction panics instead of returning an error when one of the primes is `1`. Version 0.9.10 fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
